        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.9,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a history reenactment short about tech news for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the history reenactment short \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a low-mounted tracking shot skimming just above the ground on a 50mm anamorphic with 2x squeeze, framing with rule-of-thirds weighting to frame-left with open air to the right.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with north-facing window light with a black v-flat for negative fill; grade as a filmic grade with halation on the specular highlights. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Reply with a single continuous prompt paragraph. Never explain, never bullet, never wrap it in markdown fences."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_GNBMF6YX5DRXAT8YEEHE0Q3APD",
        "kind": "text-input",
        "position": {
